/-!
# At squarefree level, divisor expansions are generated by prime ones

Theorem statement: `ModularCurve.full_eq_adjoin_primes` (`8842403e-a8ed-525d-bc7f-84e1e01e224e`), by
Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `1599ae03-e0bf-5c5e-bed5-29f4271973fb`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $N$ be a natural number, nonzero as a typeclass hypothesis, and assume $N$ is squarefree. Work
inside the field $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ of Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$, in which `jq` denotes the
Laurent series $q^{-1}$ times the rational power series `jNumQ` (the $q$-expansion of the
$j$-invariant), and in which `qExpand ℚ n` is the ring endomorphism substituting $q \mapsto q^{n}$,
obtained by multiplying exponents by $n$; thus `jqN p` $=$ `qExpand ℚ p jq` is the expansion of
$j(q^{p})$. The assertion is an equality of intermediate fields of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ over
$\mathbb{Q}$: the field `modularFunctionFieldFull N`, defined as the subfield generated over
$\mathbb{Q}$ by all the series `qExpand ℚ d jq` for nonzero divisors $d$ of $N$, coincides with the
subfield generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by `jq` together with the series `jqN p` for $p$ ranging over
the prime factors of $N$ (the nonzero condition on $p$ being automatic there).

This identifies, at squarefree level, the formal $q$-expansion model of the compositum of the
function fields of the curves $X_0(d)$, $d \mid N$, with the field generated by the prime-level
expansions alone: $\mathbb{Q}(j(q^{d}) : d \mid N) = \mathbb{Q}(j, j(q^{p}) : p \mid N)$. It is used
in the degree computations for the fields $\mathbb{Q}(j)(j(q^{N}))$, in particular by
[`ModularCurve.finrank_adjoin_jqN_eq_of_squarefree`]
(thm.html#ModularCurve.finrank_adjoin_jqN_eq_of_squarefree),
[`ModularCurve.relfinrank_adjoin_primes`](thm.html#ModularCurve.relfinrank_adjoin_primes) and
[`ModularCurve.relfinrank_full_mul_prime`](thm.html#ModularCurve.relfinrank_full_mul_prime), which
together give the degree $\psi(N)$ of the modular equation of level $N$.

